WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.400
- [Mark] All right Briana.
- [Briana] Yes.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.510
Briana, where'd you grow up?
Where are you from originally?

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.510
- [Briana] San Fernando Valley.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.527
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:22.527 --> 00:00:24.110
You had both of your parents as a kid?

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:29.110
- No. I grew up in foster care
from 14 months old, till 10.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.112
And I got adopted at 10.

00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:32.945
And-

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.340
I got adopted into like a-

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.160
She was a Catholic woman,
like a school teacher,

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.390
like totally different from my real mom

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.163
who was like a prostitute,
like a Heroin addict.

00:00:48.034 --> 00:00:51.420
And like, you know, so
it was kind of like,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.870
I don't know, the bloodlines
were different, you know.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.970
- [Mark] Very different personalities.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.690
- Yeah. Yeah.
(chuckles)

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.368
Like day night.

00:00:59.368 --> 00:01:00.272
- [Mark] And how was your,

00:01:00.272 --> 00:01:02.030
how would you describe your childhood.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:02.863
- Foster care?

00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:05.290
I mean, it was everything that
you hear about it you know.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.730
Like,

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.740
like all the bad stories, you know.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:14.740
But, at a young age I
learned that if I wasn't like

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.800
unsure about a place that
I could like run away.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.863
So I ran away a lot, in Foster care.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.163
- [Mark] What was the worst thing

00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:24.223
you had to go through yourself?

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.940
- There was this one
family that would dose us

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.860
like he doses wife with whatever he had

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.360
and he dose us, like the girls and boys.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.880
And like, you know, like have
his way with us, whatever.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.273
And I was like stuck there
for like six months because,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.810
like he was told that I ran away a lot.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.840
So I had to be like escorted to school,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.130
and like, all that shit like that,

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.453
like, it was fucked up.

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:56.290
- [Mark] So a lot of it, sounds
like a lot of sexual abuse.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.123
- Yeah.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.093
- [Mark] Does that continue
with other families?

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.250
- I mean, yeah.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.790
Like, I don't know.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.250
A lot of it happened when I was sleeping.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:10.489
So like now, like I sleep
really deep, you know.

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:13.210
I guess that happens,
like when you're a child,

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.990
and you go through that, like
you tend to block it out.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.000
Like you fall too into deep sleep,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.440
like when you're sleeping now.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.273
So-

00:02:22.654 --> 00:02:25.076
that kinda sucks you know,
when you're on the streets.

00:02:25.076 --> 00:02:26.470
(chuckles)

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.860
- [Mark] What age were you when you,

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.520
